Write a Selenium script to perform automated testing. 
Sure! Here's a simple Selenium script to perform automated testing using Python. This example will:

✅ Open a browser
✅ Navigate to Google
✅ Search for "Jenkins CI/CD"
✅ Verify the results page contains expected text

✅ Selenium Automated Test Script (Python)
🔧 Pre-requisites:
install selenium
pip install selenium

Test script
from selenium import webdriver
from selenium.webdriver.common.by import By
from selenium.webdriver.common.keys import Keys
import time

# Set up Chrome driver
driver = webdriver.Chrome()  # Make sure chromedriver is in PATH

try:
    # Step 1: Open Google
    driver.get("https://www.google.com")
    print("Opened Google homepage.")

    # Step 2: Locate search box and enter text
    search_box = driver.find_element(By.NAME, "q")
    search_box.send_keys("Jenkins CI/CD")
    search_box.send_keys(Keys.RETURN)
    print("Searched for 'Jenkins CI/CD'.")

    # Step 3: Wait for results to load
    time.sleep(2)  # better to use WebDriverWait in real tests

    # Step 4: Check if results contain "Jenkins"
    results = driver.page_source
    if "Jenkins" in results:
        print("Test Passed: 'Jenkins' found in search results.")
    else:
        print("Test Failed: 'Jenkins' not found.")

finally:
    # Step 5: Close the browser
    driver.quit()
    print("Browser closed.")


